      "side": 1,
      "message": "In `iapcontrol.cc` within `OpenDevice`, the code iterates over `hid_interfaces_` to detach kernel drivers and claim interfaces.\n\n```cpp\nerr_code \u003d libusb_claim_interface(dev_handle_ptr_.get(), hid_interfaces_[i]);\nif (err_code !\u003d 0) {\n    LogInfo(\"[IAP] {} - claim interface ({}) failed...\", ...);\n    return -1; // \u003c-- LEAK\n}\n\n```\n\nIf this fails on a subsequent interface, the function returns `-1` immediately. Previously detached kernel drivers are not re-attached, and successfully claimed interfaces are never released.\n\n* **Remediation:** Call `ReleaseResource()` before returning `-1` to ensure graceful restoration of the OS driver state.",
